    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (the suite contains the `AcceptanceTest` that asserts `timezone` = `Australia/Sydney` for an NSW owner).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived `timezone` field following the codebase's established pattern for lookup-based derived fields:\n\n1. **`model/RegionTimezones.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility lookup class mirroring `RegionPostcodes` and `CityRegions`, holding the fixed region\u2192IANA-timezone table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) with a `timezoneOf(region)` method returning `null` for regions not in the table.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTimezone()` getter that derives the timezone from the owner's existing `getLocality()` (the canonical region), reusing the region resolution already in place rather than duplicating it.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `timezone` property on the `Owner` schema, so MapStruct's existing `OwnerMapper` maps the getter into the generated `OwnerDto` automatically (no mapper changes needed).\n\nThe logic stays where it belongs: the table in its own lookup class, the derivation as a thin getter on the entity chaining off `locality`, and the API contract in the spec.",
